# Maintainer-only agent context: the working-tree layout, the cross-repository
# routine, this machine's launchers. `CLAUDE.md` IS tracked and public — anything
# that names the private repository or an absolute path on this box goes in
# `CLAUDE.local.md`, which CLAUDE.md imports and which never leaves this disk.
CLAUDE.local.md
**/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
**/.claude/

# Screenshots and crops dropped at the repository root while working on the UI.
# They are throwaway, and `git add -A` would publish them.
/*.png

# The hosted relay and its console are a separate, private service. They are
# ignored here rather than merely absent, because both directories still exist in
# a working copy split from the old monorepo — and a single `git add -A` would put
# the service back into the repository that is intended to be published. Do not
# remove these two lines to "tidy up".
/relay/
/console/

# Dispatch's design record — the argument for why it is built the way it is,
# kept locally as a maintainer note rather than published. `docs/USING-DISPATCH.md`
# is the published half and is the one to keep current; if the two ever
# disagree, the code wins. Same reasoning as CLAUDE.local.md: not every useful
# document is one the repository should ship.
/docs/DISPATCH.md

# Bytecode from the python smoke scripts in scripts/.
__pycache__/
